  "units": [
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 1,
      "source_text": "“别搞笑啦。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Stop joking around.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 2,
      "source_text": "对不再是父亲的河童和仍然是父亲的河童同等对待，那才是不合理呢。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "It would be unreasonable to treat the kappa who is no longer a father the same as the kappa who still is one.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 3,
      "source_text": "对，对，按照日本的法律，是要一视同仁的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Yes, yes, under Japanese law, they have to be treated equally.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 4,
      "source_text": "在我们看来，觉得挺搞笑的。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "From our point of view, it seems rather funny.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 5,
      "source_text": "呵呵。”",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Heh heh.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "paragraph_id": "rashomon-stories-p00944",
      "unit_index": 6,
      "source_text": "培卟扔掉烟蒂，无精打采的笑了笑。",
      "en": [
        {
          "t": "Peppu tossed away his cigarette butt and gave a listless little laugh.",
          "g": "predicate"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
